<!--
Savannah: an acacia under a low sun.

  Flat and wide, which is the whole difference between this and the
  rainforest's dome — the two sit next to each other on the picker, so the
  silhouettes have to separate at a glance. The sun is clear of the canopy;
  overlapping them turned two readable shapes into one unreadable one.

  Drawn in white and tinted at the call site with the zone's own ZoneAccent, so
  one drawable serves whatever colour the floor plan gives an area.
-->
